2 0 obj
<<
/Producer (PyPDF2)
/Title (Detecting\040gravitational\040waves\040from\040precessing\040binaries\040of\040spinning\040compact\040objects\072\040Adiabatic\040limit)
/Author (Alessandra\040Buonanno\054\040Alessandra\040Buonanno\054\040Yi\040Chen\054\040Michele\040Vallisneri)
/Subject (Black\055hole\040\050BH\051\040binaries\040with\040single\055BH\040masses\040m\075\0505\05520\051M\054\040moving\040on\040quasicircular\040orbits\054\040are\040among\040the\040most\040promising\040sources\040for\040first\055generation\040ground\055based\040gravitational\055wave\040\050GW\051\040detectors\056\040Until\040now\054\040the\040development\040of\040data\055analysis\040techniques\040to\040detect\040GWs\040from\040these\040sources\040has\040been\040focused\040mostly\040on\040nonspinning\040BHs\056\040The\040data\055analysis\040problem\040for\040the\040spinning\040case\040is\040complicated\040by\040the\040necessity\040to\040model\040the\040precession\055induced\040modulations\040of\040the\040GW\040signal\054\040and\040by\040the\040large\040number\040of\040parameters\040needed\040to\040characterize\040the\040system\054\040including\040the\040initial\040directions\040of\040the\040spins\054\040and\040the\040position\040and\040orientation\040of\040the\040binary\040with\040respect\040to\040the\040GW\040detector\056\040In\040this\040paper\040we\040consider\040binaries\040of\040maximally\040spinning\040BHs\054\040and\040we\040work\040in\040the\040adiabatic\055inspiral\040regime\040to\040build\040families\040of\040modulated\040detection\040templates\040that\040\050i\051\040are\040functions\040of\040very\040few\040physical\040and\040phenomenological\040parameters\054\040\050ii\051\040model\040remarkably\040well\040the\040dynamical\040and\040precessional\040effects\040on\040the\040GW\040signal\054\040with\040fitting\040factors\040on\040average\040greater\040than\040or\040similar\040to0\05697\054\040\050iii\051\040but\054\040however\054\040might\040require\040increasing\040the\040detection\040thresholds\054\040offsetting\040at\040least\040partially\040the\040gains\040in\040the\040fitting\040factors\056\040Our\040detection\055template\040families\040are\040quite\040promising\040also\040for\040the\040case\040of\040neutron\055star\055black\055hole\040binaries\054\040with\040fitting\040factors\040on\040average\040approximate\040to0\05693\056\040For\040these\040binaries\040we\040also\040suggest\040\050but\040do\040not\040test\051\040a\040further\040template\040family\054\040which\040would\040produce\040essentially\040exact\040waveforms\040written\040directly\040in\040terms\040of\040the\040physical\040spin\040parameters\056)
/Keywords (30\040May\0402003\054\040Physical\040Review\040D\054\040Gravitational\040wave\054\040Max\040Planck\040Society\054\040Institut\040d\047Astrophysique\040de\040Paris\054\040California\040Institute\040of\040Technology)
>>
endobj
